  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 (#500) builds `HistGradientBoostingRegressor(max_iter, learning_rate, max_depth, validation_fraction=0.1, n_iter_no_change=10, random_state=42)`; the v2 `gradientBoosting` predictor passes the same values (the last three are `non_tunable_hyperparameters`). For fewer than 10000 training pairs sklearn does not early-stop and the two are identical (`small`); with more pairs early stopping is on and both draw the validation split from `random_state=42` (`large`), so n_iter_, the train and validation scores and the predictions agree exactly.",
    "Default hyperparameters agree: 1.6.1 first grid point max_iter=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=5 (grid max_depth 5/10/30); the v2 defaults are max_iter=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=5 (space 3..30). The `defaults` variant runs the unmodified preset.",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading the CSVs (hyperparameter `gene_list`, a missing gene raises); the v2 preset selects the same list with `scaledGeneExpression(gene_list=landmark_genes)`. The synthetic gene names are in no shipped list, so both sides get a pre-selected matrix and the selection itself is not compared here.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64. HistGradientBoosting bins the features itself in float64, and the bin boundaries agree."
  ],
